+// In a coercible string, a prerelease identifier may start with a digit but
+// continue with letters, eg a commit hash like '7f3c'. The shared
+// PRERELEASEIDENTIFIER tries the numeric form first, so it would stop at the
+// first digit and the trailing guard would happily let the rest of the
+// identifier dangle ('2.3.1-nightly.7f3c' -> '2.3.1-nightly.7'). Try the
+// non-numeric form first so the whole identifier is consumed.
+createToken('COERCEPRERELEASEIDENTIFIER', `(?:${src[t.NONNUMERICIDENTIFIER]
+}|${src[t.NUMERICIDENTIFIER]})`)
